            <div xml:id="d456">

                <pb facs="0794" n="724" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg724"/>

                <head>No. 457.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Phelps to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1883-10-24"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 24, 1883</date>. (Received
                        November 17.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 21.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Mr. Iglesias came in yesterday afternoon
                    from Ancon. The city was gay with bunting, householders being required to
                    display flags.</p>
                <p>A large crowd assembled to see the arrival, and the event upon the whole may be
                    considered favorable.</p>
                <p>I have not yet received the copy of the principal articles of the treaty of
                    peace. It has been promised since Monday by a friend of Mr. Iglesias, and some
                    difficulty apparently attends procuring it.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>S. L. PHELPS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
